# --- Data policy ---
# The base synthetic dataset (data/users.csv, data/items.csv,
# data/ratings.csv) IS committed intentionally: it's generated with a
# fixed random seed (see data/generate_data.py), is small (~700 KB total),
# and committing it means a reviewer can clone the repo and go straight to
# `evaluate` / `recommend` without a required data-generation step.
#
# The train/test split and trained model artifacts, by contrast, are pure
# *derived* outputs of `python -m recsys.cli train` (deterministic given
# the seed, but regenerated on every training run) - these are ignored so
# the repo doesn't accumulate stale binary blobs across runs.
data/ratings_train.csv
data/ratings_test.csv
models/*.npz
models/*.pkl
models/config.json
models/metrics.json
